<%#
  One avatar, in one of three sizes.

  A real photo when there is one, otherwise the person's initials on a
  colour derived from their student reference — so it is the same
  colour every time and on every page, which is what makes it read as
  identity rather than decoration.

  The colour is built from one hue in HSL, so the ink is guaranteed
  readable on its own background without a palette to maintain.

  Expects: avatarUrl (or null), initials, hue, name; size = sm|md|lg.
%>
<% const _size = typeof size === "undefined" ? "md" : size; %>
<% if (avatarUrl) { %>
  <img class="sp-avatar sp-avatar-<%= _size %>" src="<%= avatarUrl %>"
       alt="<%= name %>" width="96" height="96" decoding="async">
<% } else { %>
  <span class="sp-avatar sp-avatar-<%= _size %> sp-avatar-initials" aria-hidden="true"
        style="--av-h:<%= hue %>"><%= initials %></span>
<% } %>
